<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Key features for sketching a cubic</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A sketch of \(y = {@ffac@}\) is needed.</p><p>(a) Expand \(y\).</p><div>\(y =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the \(y\)-intercept.</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the coordinates of the maximum point.</p><div>( [[input:ans3]] , [[input:ans4]] ) [[validation:ans3]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div><p>(d) Find the coordinates of the minimum point.</p><div>( [[input:ans5]] , [[input:ans6]] ) [[validation:ans5]] [[validation:ans6]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The stationary points and the intercepts are the skeleton of the curve.</p><p>(a) \(y = {@fexp@}\).</p><p>(b) Put \(x = 0\): the \(y\)-intercept is \({@yint@}\).</p><p>(c), (d) \(\dfrac{dy}{dx} = {@df@} = {@dfac@}\), which is \(0\) at \(x = {@m0@}\) and \(x = {@xs2@}\). \(\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2} = {@diff(df,x)@}\) is negative at \(x = {@xmax@}\) and positive at \(x = {@xmin@}\). The maximum point is \(({@xmax@}, {@ymax@})\) and the minimum point is \(({@xmin@}, {@ymin@})\).</p><p>The squared factor makes the curve touch the \(x\)-axis at \(x = {@m0@}\); it crosses at \(x = {@n0@}\). [[if test="is(a0>0)"]]The leading coefficient is positive, so \(y\) is large and positive for large positive \(x\), and large and negative for large negative \(x\).[[else]]The leading coefficient is negative, so \(y\) is large and negative for large positive \(x\), and large and positive for large negative \(x\).[[/if]]</p><div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Sketch of y = {#fexp#}: it touches the x-axis at ({#m0#}, 0), crosses it at ({#n0#}, 0), meets the y-axis at (0, {#yint#}), has a maximum point at ({#xmax#}, {#ymax#}) and a minimum point at ({#xmin#}, {#ymin#}).">
[[jsxgraph width="360px" height="280px"]]
(function() {
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox: [{#xl#}, {#yu+pd#}, {#xr#}, {#yl-pd#}], axis: true, grid: false, showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false, pan: {enabled: false}, zoom: {enabled: false}});
  // the curve
  b.create('functiongraph', [function(x) { return {#a0#}*(x-({#m0#}))*(x-({#m0#}))*(x-({#n0#})); }], {strokeColor: '#1f4e9c', strokeWidth: 2, fixed: true, highlight: false});
  // intercepts and stationary points
  b.create('point', [{#m0#}, 0], {name: '({#m0#}, 0)', size: 3, fixed: true, strokeColor: '#000000', fillColor: '#000000', showInfobox: false, label: {useMathJax: false, offset: [6, 12]}});
  b.create('point', [{#n0#}, 0], {name: '({#n0#}, 0)', size: 3, fixed: true, strokeColor: '#000000', fillColor: '#000000', showInfobox: false, label: {useMathJax: false, offset: [6, 12]}});
[[if test="is(xs2#0)"]]
  b.create('point', [0, {#yint#}], {name: '(0, {#yint#})', size: 3, fixed: true, strokeColor: '#000000', fillColor: '#000000', showInfobox: false, label: {useMathJax: false, offset: [8, 0]}});
[[/if]]
  b.create('point', [{#xs2#}, {#y2#}], {name: '({#xs2#}, {#y2#})', size: 3, fixed: true, strokeColor: '#000000', fillColor: '#000000', showInfobox: false, label: {useMathJax: false, offset: [8, 8]}});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
